WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.420
What about Activator?

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.519
Fabric has a dedicated tool called

00:00:03.519 --> 00:00:05.620
data Activator specifically for triggering

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.979
actions based on data changes.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.000
If I write a natural language

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
business rule in my ontology interface,

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.059
does that automatically provision an

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:15.659
Activator alert in the background?

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.900
No, it absolutely does not.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.420
And that's a massive point of

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.600
confusion for new users.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.940
Saving a natural language role in

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.820
the ontology provides semantic context

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:25.960
for the chat agents.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.220
It does not automatically write the

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.020
code to provision an active running

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.620
workflow in data Activator.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.460
So they are separate steps.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.940
If you want an alert to

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.920
actually fire, a data engineer has

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.640
to go into Activator and configure

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.380
that automation separately against

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.559
the supported data path.
